{
  "_about": [
    "Documentation category path -> product area, for B1 (codebase staleness).",
    "",
    "The doc platform's own category tree is authored by the documentation team and is a better",
    "description of the doc side than anything derived: fixtures/code-areas.json had to be inferred",
    "from graph communities because nothing authoritative existed. This is authoritative.",
    "",
    "HAND-ASSIGNED, like fixtures/taxonomy.json and for the same reason. 85 paths onto 14 areas is",
    "a sitting an afternoon, not a modelling problem, and a wrong label here silently mis-routes",
    "every article beneath it.",
    "",
    "A path may map to SEVERAL areas. 'Reports in Boards' is genuinely both boards-cases and",
    "reports-analytics, and forcing a single tag would hide it from one of the two searches that",
    "should find it.",
    "",
    "`unmapped` is deliberate and is NOT a todo list. An entry there has no honest single area, and",
    "leaving it untagged means a code change never raises it — which is correct for a podcast, a",
    "discontinued-services note, or a glossary whose area varies per term."
  ],
